WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:03.120
One misconception
of meditation is

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.270
that if you're meditating
your mind will be blank.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:08.440
You can't make your mind blank.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.350
And if you try, you're
just going to wind up

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.687
with a gigantic headache.

00:00:11.687 --> 00:00:12.472
[LAUGHS]

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.970
In a way, when
we're on autopilot,

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:20.440
we're sleepwalking
through our lives.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:25.030
Mindfulness is traditionally
a form of meditation.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:29.260
It's the awareness that
arises from paying attention

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:34.180
on purpose in the present
moment and nonjudgmentally.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:39.350
If you're breathing, this
class could be for you.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.390
I've been committed
to mindfulness

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.370
for well over 50 years.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.990
It's a way in which you
could take care of your body,

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.360
take care of your mind.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.970
And that's what this
is really about.

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:54.690
The entire thrust
of this MasterClass

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.400
is not about attaining.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.610
It's about recognizing
you're already whole.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.880
When you set about bringing
mindfulness into your life,

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:07.320
the best coping strategy
is to recognize stress

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.770
and how to minimize
our reactivity

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.870
to those stressors, no
matter how stressful,

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:13.890
no matter how painful.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.470
I could ground myself
in the present moment.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.760
Stop, remember,

00:01:18.843 --> 00:01:19.926
drop.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:25.120
We can cultivate mindfulness
in an array of different ways.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.120
And the beauty of
meditation is some forms

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.800
will resonate with some people.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:33.160
And other forms will resonate
differently with other people.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.220
I do not consider this
to be a master class.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:38.440
This is not about mastery.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:39.850
I'm not the curriculum.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.660
You're the curriculum.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:46.090
This is an invitation to
befriend yourself and sign up

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.320
for the adventure of a lifetime.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.335
This is Jon Kabat-Zinn, and
this is my non-MasterClass.

00:01:52.335 --> 00:01:54.680
[MUSIC PLAYING]

